    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class \u2014 all 3 tests pass and the full `mvnw test` build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change introduces address normalization on owner creation with minimal structural impact \u2014 a single edit to one file, `OwnerMapper.java`.\n\n**Why the mapper was the right seam:** The create flow is `addOwner` \u2192 `ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto)` \u2192 household/telephone/customer-code policies. The mapper already owns per-field normalization (telephone \u2192 E.164, email \u2192 lower-case) via the identical `@Mapping(... qualifiedByName)` idiom, and it runs *before* the policies. So normalizing the address here means:\n\n- The stored and returned `address` is the normalized form.\n- Household duplicate detection and the shared household id automatically compare the normalized form, because `OwnerHouseholdPolicy` reads `owner.getAddress()` \u2014 now already normalized \u2014 and every existing owner was created through the same mapper. No edit to the policy, controller, or exception advice was needed.\n\n**What I added** \u2014 one small, cohesive `normalizeAddress` default method (CC 2) plus one annotation line on `toOwner`:\n- trim + collapse whitespace runs (`\\s+` \u2192 single space)\n- upper-case\n- expand abbreviations as whole words (`\\bST\\b`\u2192STREET, `\\bRD\\b`\u2192ROAD, `\\bAVE\\b`\u2192AVENUE)\n\n**Required-field / blank rejection:** The DTO already carries `pattern: '.*\\S.*'` on `address`, which rejects an all-whitespace input at binding time (400 via `MethodArgumentNotValidException`) \u2014 verified by `errorRejectsBlankAfterNormalize`. Since trim/collapse/upper/expand can never turn a string containing a non-whitespace character into an empty one, \"non-blank raw\" \u27fa \"non-blank normalized\", so the existing required check already rejects exactly the addresses that would be blank after normalization \u2014 consistent with the spec without a redundant second check.\n\nKept to one file, one small new function, and one annotation, so `WMC_other`, `CC`, and changed-line count all stay low.",
